.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
#include \f[B]<bashclient.h>\f[R]

#define BC_OBSERVE_LEVEL_OFF      0
#define BC_OBSERVE_LEVEL_COMMAND  1

int bc_observe_subscribe(bc_client_t *c, int level);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Subscribes the client to command observation events on
\f[CR]CHAN_OBSERVE\f[R] (channel 3).
After a successful subscription, the server will push pre\-command and
post\-command event messages whenever the bash interpreter executes
commands.
.PP
The function sends a v2 JSON request on the control channel to set the
observe level, then waits for the server\(cqs acknowledgement.
.PP
