.TE
.PP
After subscribing, events are not delivered automatically.
The caller must invoke \f[CR]bc_poll()\f[R] in a loop to receive and
dispatch events to registered callbacks.
Events that arrive before callbacks are registered are silently
discarded.
.PP
A typical usage pattern is:
.IP "1." 3
Register callbacks with \f[CR]bc_observe_on_pre_command()\f[R] and/or
\f[CR]bc_observe_on_post_command()\f[R].
.IP "2." 3
Call \f[CR]bc_observe_subscribe(c, BC_OBSERVE_LEVEL_COMMAND)\f[R].
.IP "3." 3
Execute commands via \f[CR]bc_eval()\f[R].
.IP "4." 3
Call \f[CR]bc_poll()\f[R] to process incoming events.
.PP
Calling \f[CR]bc_observe_subscribe()\f[R] with level 1 when already
subscribed at level 1 is a no\-op on the server side and returns
\f[CR]BC_OK\f[R].
