.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
The subscription state is per\-session.
Each authenticated session has its own independent observation level.
.IP \(bu 2
Events are serialized as JSON on \f[CR]CHAN_OBSERVE\f[R] and decoded by
the client library before dispatch to callbacks.
.IP \(bu 2
The server clamps out\-of\-range levels silently; the client library
validates the level parameter before sending the request and returns
\f[CR]BC_ERR_PARAM\f[R] for invalid values.
.IP \(bu 2
Subscribing at level 0 is equivalent to unsubscribing and is a valid
operation.
.IP \(bu 2
The function blocks until the server acknowledges the level change.
Use \f[CR]bc_poll()\f[R] for event processing, not for the subscription
handshake itself.
.IP \(bu 2
Thread safety: the client library is not thread\-safe.
Do not call \f[CR]bc_observe_subscribe()\f[R] concurrently with other
operations on the same \f[CR]bc_client_t\f[R].
